Fix mt7925u AP-mode TX headroom underflow (kernel panic).

mt7925_usb_sdio_tx_prepare_skb() writes the TXWI at skb->data -
MT_SDIO_TXD_SIZE and then skb_push()es it, but unlike the sibling
mt7921_usb_sdio_tx_prepare_skb() it never calls skb_cow_head() first. When
mac80211 hands the driver a skb without enough headroom (the beacon path in
AP mode), skb_push() walks below skb->head and trips skb_under_panic():

  skbuff: skb_under_panic: text:ffffffffc0fadea9 len:409 put:
  kernel BUG at net/core/skbuff.c:212!
  Call Trace:
   mt7925_usb_sdio_tx_prepare_skb+0xc9/0x170 [mt7925_common]
   mt76u_tx_queue_skb+0x8d/0x1f0 [mt76_usb]

Guarantee the headroom up front, exactly as mt7921 does.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7925/mac.c
@@ -1422,6 +1422,10 @@ int mt7925_usb_sdio_tx_prepare_skb(struct mt76_dev *mdev, void *txwi_ptr,
 	if (unlikely(tx_info->skb->len <= ETH_HLEN))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	err = skb_cow_head(skb, MT_SDIO_TXD_SIZE + MT_SDIO_HDR_SIZE);
+	if (err)
+		return err;
+
 	if (!wcid)
 		wcid = &dev->mt76.global_wcid;
